CUDA math policy (cuda_fast_math): fast
HIP math policy (hip_fast_math): fast
f32 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt of +-0, +-inf and NaN: NaN where f64 gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity f64 gives, or within the stated ulps of it (every backend): true
f32 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt of finite nonzero inputs: within the stated ulps of f64 with subnormals kept (skipped on Metal and on CUDA's f32 intrinsics under --use_fast_math, accepted vendor behaviour claimed by their own contracts): true
Metal f32 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt: NaN where f64 gives NaN, the signed zero or infinity where f64 rounds to one, otherwise within the stated ulps of f64 -- for exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt, of f64 at the input or the f32 result flushed from subnormal to zero: true
f32 pow and fmod over +-0, +-inf, NaN and dyadic operands: NaN where C gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity C gives, or within the stated ulps of it -- CUDA's f32 pow under --use_fast_math within __powf's 2 + 2 |y log2 |x|| -- and fmod exactly (every backend): true
f32 fmod of constant operands, folded on the host: exactly C's fmod, the remainder taking the sign of the dividend under a negative modulus too (every backend): true
CUDA f32 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt under --use_fast_math: within the fast intrinsics' contracts -- sin and cos absolute 2^-21.41 (plus 2^-23 |x| past pi) below 2^22 and any value in [-1, 1] from there, tanh relative 2^-10.987, exp 2 + 1.173 |x| ulps, log and log2 absolute 2^-21.41 and 2^-22 on [0.5, 2] and the stated ulps elsewhere, f32 subnormals flushed: true
half sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt of +-0, +-inf and NaN: NaN where f64 gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity f64 gives, or within the stated ulps of it (every backend): true
half sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt of finite nonzero inputs: within the stated ulps of f64 with subnormals kept (skipped on Metal and on CUDA's f32 intrinsics under --use_fast_math, accepted vendor behaviour claimed by their own contracts): true
Metal half sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt: NaN where f64 gives NaN, the signed zero or infinity where f64 rounds to one, otherwise within the stated ulps of f64 -- for exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt, of f64 at the input or the f32 result flushed from subnormal to zero: true
half pow and fmod over +-0, +-inf, NaN and dyadic operands: NaN where C gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity C gives, or within the stated ulps of it -- CUDA's f32 pow under --use_fast_math within __powf's 2 + 2 |y log2 |x|| -- and fmod exactly (every backend): true
half fmod of constant operands, folded on the host: exactly C's fmod, the remainder taking the sign of the dividend under a negative modulus too (every backend): true
bfloat16 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt of +-0, +-inf and NaN: NaN where f64 gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity f64 gives, or within the stated ulps of it (every backend): true
bfloat16 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt of finite nonzero inputs: within the stated ulps of f64 with subnormals kept (skipped on Metal and on CUDA's f32 intrinsics under --use_fast_math, accepted vendor behaviour claimed by their own contracts): true
Metal bfloat16 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt: NaN where f64 gives NaN, the signed zero or infinity where f64 rounds to one, otherwise within the stated ulps of f64 -- for exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt, of f64 at the input or the f32 result flushed from subnormal to zero: true
bfloat16 pow and fmod over +-0, +-inf, NaN and dyadic operands: NaN where C gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity C gives, or within the stated ulps of it -- CUDA's f32 pow under --use_fast_math within __powf's 2 + 2 |y log2 |x|| -- and fmod exactly (every backend): true
bfloat16 fmod of constant operands, folded on the host: exactly C's fmod, the remainder taking the sign of the dividend under a negative modulus too (every backend): true
CUDA bfloat16 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt under --use_fast_math: within the fast intrinsics' contracts -- sin and cos absolute 2^-21.41 (plus 2^-23 |x| past pi) below 2^22 and any value in [-1, 1] from there, tanh relative 2^-10.987, exp 2 + 1.173 |x| ulps, log and log2 absolute 2^-21.41 and 2^-22 on [0.5, 2] and the stated ulps elsewhere, f32 subnormals flushed: true
f32 log and log2 have the sign of x - 1 on every f32 within 2^-13 of 1, and are +0 at 1 -- Box-Muller's sqrt (-2 log u) needs log u <= 0 (every backend): true
f32 log and log2 on every f32 within 2^-13 of 1: within the backend's contract -- the stated ulps of f64, CUDA's absolute 2^-21.41 and 2^-22 under --use_fast_math (every backend): true
f64 sqrt and rsqrt of +-0, +-inf and NaN: NaN where f64 gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity f64 gives (skipped on Metal, which has no f64): true
f64 sqrt and rsqrt of finite nonzero inputs, subnormals among them: within the stated ulps of the host's f64 (1 for sqrt, 2 for rsqrt) with subnormals kept (skipped on Metal, which has no f64): true
f64 pow and fmod over +-0, +-inf, NaN, dyadic and subnormal operands: NaN where C gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity C gives, and fmod exactly (skipped on Metal, which has no f64): true
f64 pow's finite nonzero results over the same operands: within 2 ulps of C's pow (skipped on Metal, which has no f64, and on HIP under hip_fast_math, whose pow under -ffp-contract=fast loses the low part of its extended-precision y log x, claimed by the next line): true
HIP f64 pow's finite nonzero results over the same operands under hip_fast_math: within 2 + 2 |y log2 |x|| ulps of C's pow: true
f64 fmod of constant operands, subnormal ones among them, folded on the host: exactly C's fmod (skipped on Metal, which has no f64): true
